# KUBRIQUE-M — Far-Future Vehicle Profile (Concept Only)

KUBRIQUE-M is a large-scale, far-future conceptual extension of the KUBRIQUE 
architecture. It imagines what a high-capacity, long-duration hypersonic 
vehicle might look like if next-generation materials, ultra-high-temperature 
structures, and advanced detonation-based propulsion technologies become 
available.

This profile is **not** an engineering specification and contains no 
manufacturing information. It is intended for safe educational and imaginative 
use.

---

## 1. Mission Concept

KUBRIQUE-M is envisioned for:

• long-range hypersonic transport  
• high-mass suborbital delivery  
• conceptual surface-to-orbit operations  
• Mars atmospheric ascent/descent studies  
• future heavy-lift variants of the KUBRIQUE system  

It serves as a “big sibling” reference for scaling the KUBRIQUE architecture.

---

## 2. Visual & Structural Concept

KUBRIQUE-M preserves the signature KUBRIQUE features:

• Cylindrical “can” architecture  
• Annular collar regions (scaled up)  
• Central rocket core channel (larger volume)  
• Expanded propellant volumes  
• Reinforced thermal protection regions  
• Multi-ring collar system (for artistic representation)  

No internal structures, wall thicknesses, or engineering tolerances are 
included.

---

## 3. Propulsion Concept (Non-Functional)

The vehicle explores speculative future propulsion ideas:

• multiple conceptual annular detonation rings  
• multi-band inlet regions  
• high-level energy transfer layers  
• conceptual high-altitude rocket augmentation  

These are **visual placeholders** only and cannot be manufactured.

---

## 4. Scaling Philosophy

KUBRIQUE-M is used to:

• explore larger geometries  
• test visual proportions  
• examine multi-ring stacking  
• expand the architecture’s identity  
• inspire sci-fi or technical illustrations  

It demonstrates how KUBRIQUE can evolve in a modular, scalable fashion.
